<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 5.8 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 5.8 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 5.8 percent in the week to June 25 over the equivalent week a year ago, figures from the Bank of England showed. Last week the rise was 6.4 percent.  </p>
<p>(figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>		     Latest week  Previous week year-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation  21.67    21.60    20.48</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	 2.65     2.55     1.83</p>
</text>
